%% Inclusive hierarchical caching: KV blocks evicted from HBM cascade into
%% the secondary fast memory pool; cold blocks demote further to host DRAM.
%% Hot/popular blocks stay in the smaller fast pool; everything else lives
%% in the larger slow pool. See docs/design/rfcs/inclusive-hierarchical-caching.md
flowchart TB
    HBM["HBM<br/>GPU KV cache<br/>both hot and warm blocks"]:::hbm

    Fast["Secondary fast memory pool<br/>caches HOT blocks evicted from HBM<br/>high reuse rate"]:::fast
    Slow["Slow host DRAM pool<br/>caches BOTH hot and warm blocks<br/>superset, includes everything fast holds"]:::slow

    HBM ==>|evict cascade| Fast
    HBM ==>|evict cascade| Slow
    Fast -->|"demote on fast eviction (LRU)"| Slow
    Slow -->|"promote on hot reuse (if room in fast)"| Fast

    classDef hbm fill:#fff3e6,stroke:#cc6600,stroke-width:2px
    classDef fast fill:#e8f5e0,stroke:#3a8a1a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef slow fill:#e6f0ff,stroke:#1a4d99,stroke-width:2px
